== Redlink policy ==

The wave intentionally exposes normalized prerequisites such as:

[[Syntax]], [[Pragmatics]], [[Class]], [[Instance]], [[Type]], [[Predicate]], [[Graph]], [[Identifier]], [[Internationalized Resource Identifier]], [[RDF Schema]], [[SPARQL]], [[SHACL]], [[SKOS]], [[Linked Data]], [[Logical entailment]], [[Soundness]], [[Completeness]], [[Satisfiability]], [[Open-world assumption]], [[Closed-world assumption]], [[Entity resolution]].

These are coverage signals, not automatic stub requests.

== Acceptance criteria ==

Wave 2 is ready to leave Phase 3 when:

# all 60 surfaces remain present;
# one concept = one Core semantic identity;
# controlled domains pass;
# public/project distinctions remain explicit;
# all depth derivatives remain category/identity-exempt;
# slash-title deployment mapping remains valid;
# <code>validate_v2.py</code> passes;
# runtime-schema, substrate, deployment, workflow and Main-space audits pass;
# staging builds the complete stacked graph.

